    "response": "{\"decision\":\"established_flaw\",\"issues\":[{\"category\":\"unsupported_inference\",\"target_kind\":\"assertion\",\"claim_quote\":\"The displayed sources show that policy debate is mainly driven by institutional procedures and formal paperwork.\",\"evidence\":[{\"excerpt_id\":\"EXC_c618fdd3d1bf53c7\",\"quote\":\"I strongly support the work that the Home Secretary has done with regard to controlling bogus student visa applications. That was a huge problem that she has got rid of.\"}],\"whole_packet_no_support\":\"absence of evidence demonstrating institutional procedures as the *main* driver of debate; the sources discuss visa applications, student numbers, and business support for migration, not procedural dominance.\",\"mechanism\":\"Misrepresentation of evidence scope; selective presentation of data.\",\"material_consequence\":\"The claim oversimplifies the complex factors influencing policy debate, ignoring diverse perspectives and concerns.\",\"counterconditions\":\"The evidence highlights support for migration, business perspectives, and specific policy interventions, indicating a broader range of influences than solely institutional procedures.\"}],\"unresolved\":[],\"rationale\":\"The provided sources contain numerous references to immigration policy, business support, and individual constituent concerns, directly contradicting the claim that institutional procedures and paperwork are *mainly* driving policy debate. The evidence demonstrates a more multifaceted landscape of influences.\"}",
